## 🔍 Casos de Uso Comunes

### **Caso 1: Descubrir Roles Custom**

```powershell
# Extraer todos los roles
.\PIM-SecureAssignment-ARM.ps1 -ExtractRoles -SupportAzureRBAC -ExportRolesCsv

# Filtrar roles custom
$roles = Import-Csv "roles_reference.csv"
$customRoles = $roles | Where-Object { $_.IsCustom -eq 'True' -and $_.Type -eq 'Azure RBAC' }

Write-Host "Roles Custom encontrados:" -ForegroundColor Cyan
$customRoles | Format-Table DisplayName, RoleDefinitionId

# Agregar a lista blanca del script
foreach ($role in $customRoles) {
    Write-Host "'$($role.RoleDefinitionId)' = @{ Name = '$($role.DisplayName)'; MaxDuration = 'P7D'; RequiresApproval = `$true }"
}
```

---

### **Caso 2: Migración Masiva con Detección de Herencia**

```powershell
# Paso 1: Identificar usuarios con Owner en suscripción
$ownerRoleId = "8e3af657-a8ff-443c-a75c-2fe8c4bcb635"
$subScope = "/subscriptions/xxx"

$owners = Get-AzRoleAssignment -Scope $subScope -RoleDefinitionId $ownerRoleId

# Paso 2: Generar CSV
$migrations = $owners | ForEach-Object {
    [PSCustomObject]@{
        PrincipalId = $_.ObjectId
        RoleDefinitionId = ''
        DirectoryScopeId = ''
        AzureRoleDefinitionId = $ownerRoleId
        AzureScope = $subScope
        GroupId = ''
        Reason = "MIGRATION-2025: Conversión Owner a PIM"
        Duration = 'PT4H'
    }
}

$migrations | Export-Csv "migration_owners.csv" -NoTypeInformation

# Paso 3: Dry-Run para ver herencia
.\PIM-SecureAssignment-ARM.ps1 -CsvPath "migration_owners.csv" -Phase 1 -SupportAzureRBAC -AutoMigrate -DryRun

# El script detectará automáticamente:
# - Asignaciones en el scope exacto
# - Asignaciones heredadas desde management groups
# - Asignaciones redundantes en RGs hijos

# Paso 4: Ejecutar migración
.\PIM-SecureAssignment-ARM.ps1 -CsvPath "migration_owners.csv" -Phase 1 -SupportAzureRBAC -AutoMigrate
```

---

### **Caso 3: Validar CSV Antes de Ejecutar**

```powershell
# Extraer roles de referencia
.\PIM-SecureAssignment-ARM.ps1 -ExtractRoles -SupportAzureRBAC -ExportRolesCsv

# Validar GUIDs en tu CSV
$csv = Import-Csv "assignments.csv"
$rolesRef = Import-Csv "roles_reference.csv"

$errors = 0
foreach ($row in $csv) {
    if ($row.AzureRoleDefinitionId) {
        $exists = $rolesRef | Where-Object { 
            $_.RoleDefinitionId -eq $row.AzureRoleDefinitionId 
        }
        
        if (-not $exists) {
            Write-Host "❌ GUID inválido: $($row.AzureRoleDefinitionId)" -ForegroundColor Red
            $errors++
        }
        else {
            Write-Host "✓ $($exists.DisplayName)" -ForegroundColor Green
        }
    }
}

if ($errors -eq 0) {
    Write-Host "`n✓ CSV válido. Listo para ejecutar." -ForegroundColor Green
}
else {
    Write-Host "`n⚠️  $errors errores encontrados. Corregir antes de ejecutar." -ForegroundColor Yellow
}
```

